import DisplayEquation from '../../components/DisplayEquation.astro';

const differentialForm = String.raw`\frac{\partial u}{\partial t} + \nabla \cdot F(u) = 0`;
const integralForm = String.raw`\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t} \int_\Omega u\,\mathrm{d}V = -\int_{\partial\Omega} F(u) \cdot n\,\mathrm{d}S`;
---

<p>
  A conservation law tracks a quantity such as mass or charge. Without sources,
  the amount in a region changes only when the quantity flows across its
  boundary.
</p>

<DisplayEquation tex={differentialForm} />

<p>
  Here <var>u</var> is the conserved quantity per unit volume, and <var>F</var>(
  <var>u</var>) is its flux. A positive flux divergence means more leaves a
  small region than enters, so the local density decreases.
</p>

<div>
  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-oiseau-light-text">
    Balance over a region
  </h3>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Integrating over a fixed region Ω gives the rate of change of the total
    amount. The minus sign makes outward flux a loss. The vector <var>n</var> is
    the outward unit normal on the boundary ∂Ω.
  </p>
  <DisplayEquation tex={integralForm} class="mt-3" />
</div>

<div>
  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-oiseau-light-text">
    How DG applies the balance
  </h3>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Oiseau represents the solution by a polynomial in each mesh element. At a
    shared face, a numerical flux uses the solution values from both sides. A
    conservative numerical flux assigns equal and opposite transfers to the two
    elements, so internal face fluxes cancel when the element balances are
    summed.
  </p>
</div>
